From d3a80bdca15fd914be453d382789904432057518 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vadik likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 23:58:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: arm64: avoid cache maintenance on assigned MMIO

The protected-device donation path maps an MMIO aperture with Device
attributes and then performs cache maintenance by VA on its first page.
Tegra234 forwards that operation to the device fabric, which reports an
uncorrectable CBB error for every MGBE resource and locks the host before
device reset can run.

MMIO mappings do not allocate cache lines. Remove the cache operation so
donation only changes ownership and the trusted reset remains the first
EL2 device access.
---
 arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c
index fb04b567d..e1d0f5562 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/device/device.c
@@ -120,9 +120,6 @@ int pkvm_device_hyp_assign_mmio(u64 pfn, u64 nr_pages)
 	}
 
 	ret = pkvm_host_donate_hyp_mmio(pfn, nr_pages, PAGE_HYP_DEVICE);
-	/* Hyp have device mapping, while host may have issue cacheable writes.*/
-	if (!ret)
-		kvm_flush_dcache_to_poc(__hyp_va(phys), PAGE_SIZE);
 
 out_unlock:
 	hyp_spin_unlock(&device_spinlock);
-- 
2.55.0

